Form / Simple-Request Content-Type Rejection (415 UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE):
If the request has a body (content-length > 0 or transfer-encoding present), content-type must start with application/json (case-insensitive, parameters such as ; charset=utf-8 permitted). application/x-www-form-urlencoded, multipart/form-data, and text/plain are unconditionally rejected with 415 UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE before body parsing. Bodyless unsafe requests (POST /api/v1/auth/logout, DELETE /api/v1/calendar/session, DELETE /api/v1/me/bookmarks/:id) require no Content-Type if content-length is 0/absent, or application/json if provided.
Strict Origin / Referer Allowlist Check (403 CSRF_ORIGIN_DENIED / 403 CSRF_ORIGIN_REQUIRED):
If Origin header is present:
Origin: null or malformed URL → 403 CSRF_ORIGIN_DENIED.
Normalized origin not in CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS → 403 CSRF_ORIGIN_DENIED (even if X-CSRF-Token is valid).
Else if Referer header is present:
Parse new URL(referer).origin; malformed URL or origin not in CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS → 403 CSRF_ORIGIN_DENIED.
Else (both Origin and Referer absent):
403 CSRF_ORIGIN_REQUIRED. (Browsers always send Origin on POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE fetch() calls; rejecting missing Origin+Referer closes Referrer-Policy: no-referrer stripping attacks).
Cryptographic X-CSRF-Token Verification (403 CSRF_TOKEN_MISSING / 403 CSRF_TOKEN_INVALID / 403 CSRF_TOKEN_EXPIRED):
Resolve subjectBinding from request.cookies (§3.2) and validate X-CSRF-Token via crypto.timingSafeEqual. X-Requested-With is never accepted as a substitute.
