8. WP3 — CORS Preflight Cache Correctness
Classification: Confirmed defect in Revision 1.0 Vary specification corrected.
8.1 Exact Vary Header Split (src/routes/middleware/http-security.ts)
Non-OPTIONS Responses (All Standard API Requests):
Append Origin to Vary (Vary: Origin, deduplicated case-insensitively with any existing Vary tokens) on every response regardless of whether Origin matched, was absent, or was denied, preventing shared caches from serving an origin-specific Access-Control-Allow-Origin header to another origin.
OPTIONS Responses (All Preflight & Non-CORS OPTIONS Requests):
Always emit:
code
Http
Vary: Origin, Access-Control-Request-Method, Access-Control-Request-Headers
Including all three request headers on both allowed (204) and denied (403) OPTIONS responses guarantees intermediary/browser caches partition cached preflight entries by origin, target HTTP method, and requested header set.
8.2 Preflight Validation, Cache Policy & Access-Control-Max-Age: 600 Analysis
Allowed Preflight Criteria:
Origin header is present and exact-matches CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS.
Access-Control-Request-Method is present and matches GET | HEAD | POST | PUT | PATCH | DELETE | OPTIONS.
Every comma-separated token in Access-Control-Request-Headers (if present), trimmed and lowercased, belongs to the explicit allowlist: content-type, x-csrf-token, x-request-id, x-calendar-session, accept.
Allowed Preflight Response (204 No Content):
Access-Control-Allow-Origin: <exact matched Origin> (never *)
Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true
Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, HEAD, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS
Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Content-Type, X-CSRF-Token, X-Request-ID, X-Calendar-Session, Accept
Access-Control-Max-Age: 600
Cache-Control: private, max-age=600
Vary: Origin, Access-Control-Request-Method, Access-Control-Request-Headers
Why Access-Control-Max-Age: 600 + Cache-Control: private, max-age=600 Is Safe:
600s (10 minutes) eliminates repetitive OPTIONS round-trips before POST/PATCH/DELETE mutations carrying X-CSRF-Token (within Chromium's 7200s cap and Firefox's 86400s cap), while bounding CORS policy revocation propagation to at most 10 minutes after a config rollback.
Cache-Control: private, max-age=600 permits the end-user browser's internal CORS preflight cache to honor Access-Control-Max-Age: 600 while forbidding shared CDNs/reverse proxies from caching preflight responses across users.
Disallowed Preflight Response (403 Forbidden):
Emits zero Access-Control-Allow-* headers, Cache-Control: no-store, Vary: Origin, Access-Control-Request-Method, Access-Control-Request-Headers, and standard JSON { error: { code: 'CORS_ORIGIN_DENIED' | 'CORS_PREFLIGHT_DENIED', ... } }.
