Classification: Confirmed deployment hazard in Revision 1.0 HSTS default corrected.
9.1 Repository Audit of CANONICAL_DOMAIN & Subdomain Topology
src/config/env.ts:87-91 defaults CANONICAL_DOMAIN to 'http://localhost:3000' and validates in production (lines 204-213) only that it is a valid non-localhost URL (for example https://elimupin.co.ke in tests/db/config.test.ts:7).
src/services/seo.service.ts:65, 78-86 uses CANONICAL_DOMAIN to construct public canonical page URLs and sitemaps—commonly an apex/registrable domain (elimupin.co.ke).
Hazard of Revision 1.0 Default (max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains):
Emitting includeSubDomains from an apex host pins every subdomain (*.elimupin.co.ke) to HTTPS for 1 year in visitors' browsers, breaking any non-HTTPS staging, internal tool, or legacy subdomain.
Emitting a 1-year max-age before HTTPS termination is verified in production risks long-lived client lockout; furthermore, RFC 6797 §7.2 forbids sending Strict-Transport-Security over plaintext HTTP.
9.2 Safe HSTS Rollout Policy & API Security Headers
HSTS Environment Controls (src/config/env.ts):
HSTS_MAX_AGE_SECONDS: integer 0..63072000, default 300 (5 minutes — OWASP recommended initial rollout stage; setting 0 disables app-layer HSTS if TLS edge proxy manages HSTS).
HSTS_INCLUDE_SUBDOMAINS: boolean ('true' | 'false'), default false (never enabled unless operator has audited HTTPS across all subdomains). preload is never emitted automatically.
Strict Emission Gate (RFC 6797 §7.2 Compliant):
Strict-Transport-Security is emitted if and only if:
effectiveNodeEnv === 'production', AND
env.HSTS_MAX_AGE_SECONDS > 0, AND
env.CANONICAL_DOMAIN.startsWith('https://'), AND
request.protocol === 'https' (resolved safely via Wave 1's bounded resolveEffectiveTrustProxy hop count!).
Header value when all four hold: max-age=${env.HSTS_MAX_AGE_SECONDS}${env.HSTS_INCLUDE_SUBDOMAINS ? '; includeSubDomains' : ''}.
Operators graduate HSTS_MAX_AGE_SECONDS (300 → 86400 → 2592000 → 31536000) solely via environment config after verifying TLS health.
API-Only Security Headers (src/routes/middleware/http-security.ts):
X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
X-Frame-Options: DENY
Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-site
Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none' — explicitly scoped to this Fastify API server's JSON/XML/text responses (preventing content-sniffed script execution or framing if an API URL is navigated to directly). Documented in docs/SECURITY_RULES.md as distinct from any separate frontend HTML document CSP.
